.TH PLANSPLEASE 1 "October 2026" "plansplease" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
plansplease \- publish and upload immutable HTML snapshots
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B plansplease
.RI [ global-options ]
.I command
[\fIoptions\fR]
.br
.B plansplease help
[\fIcommand\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B plansplease
uses the existing local profiles, documents, credentials, and daemon.
The npm package, local data paths, and PLANVIEW environment settings retain their existing names.
.PP
.B plansplease
publishes an HTML file or page folder to a local daemon and returns a stable
localhost URL. It can also upload an HTML file or artifact folder to the cloud workspace.
A page folder must contain
.B index.html
and is published with its assets.
.PP
Use
.B --profile name
before the command to use an isolated set of documents and daemon state.
The default profile keeps the existing Planview data directory. Named profiles
are stored below
.B planview/profiles/name
.
.PP
The
.B publish
command creates a snapshot and prints its URL. Pass
.B \-\-open
to open the URL in the default browser after publishing.
.PP
Use
.B login
before
.B upload
to authorize this computer in a browser. Cloud preview links require the same
account to be signed in in the browser.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B publish [options] file|folder
Publish an immutable HTML snapshot and print its URL. Use
.B \-\-open
to open the URL in the default browser.
.TP
.B login [options]
Open the selected app's account sign-in in a browser and authorize this computer.
Hosted apps use GitHub sign-in; the local workspace uses its local test account. Use
.B \-\-cloud-url origin
to sign in to another app origin.
.TP
.B logout
Revoke the saved cloud sign-in on the app, then remove it from this computer.
Revocation requires a connection.
.TP
.B upload [options] file.html|folder
Upload an HTML file or artifact folder and print its workspace preview URL. Folders require index.html, at most 512 files, and 8 MiB including the manifest.
The preview requires an authenticated browser session.
.TP
.B get id|url
Write a stored snapshot's exact bytes to standard output. The reference must be
a document id or an exact local preview URL.
.TP
.B start [options]
Start the local daemon, or reuse the authenticated daemon already running.
.TP
.B status [options]
Show daemon status without starting a daemon.
.TP
.B stop [options]
Gracefully stop the local daemon.
.TP
.B restart [options]
Restart the local daemon.
.TP
.B clean [options]
Remove expired snapshots and reconcile incomplete storage operations.
.TP
.B help [command]
Show help for the whole CLI or for one command.
.SH AGENT SKILLS
Install Planview's skills with the Vercel Skills CLI from a project directory:
.EX
npx skills add https://github.com/abijith-suresh/planview/tree/main/apps/cli/skills
.EE
From a Planview checkout, use
.B npx skills add ./apps/cli/skills
instead. Skills CLI installs to the project by default; use
.B \-g
for optional user-wide installation. Use
.B \-a codex \-y
for a non-interactive Codex install.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show the relevant help text. Use
.B plansplease help command
to request help explicitly.
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-version
Show the plansplease CLI version.
.TP
.B \-\-profile name
Use the named profile for this invocation. Names start with a lowercase letter
or number and contain only lowercase letters, numbers, hyphens, and underscores.
.TP
.B \-\-open
Open the returned URL in the default browser. Supported by
.B publish
and
.B upload
.
.TP
.B \-\-cloud-url origin
Select the cloud app origin for
.B login
.
.TP
.B PLANVIEW_CLOUD_URL
Environment variable selecting the default cloud app origin for
.B login
.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print one newline-terminated JSON object for metadata commands. Supported by
.B publish
,
.B start
,
.B status
,
.B stop
,
.B restart
,
and
.B clean
,
.B upload
.
.TP
.B \-\-
Stop option parsing. Text after this marker is treated as an operand.
.SH OUTPUT
Successful text output goes to standard output. Errors go to standard error.
.B get
writes only the stored document bytes to standard output.
.PP
With
.B \-\-json
, successful metadata commands write one JSON object followed by a newline.
JSON errors use an
.B error
object on standard error. The
.B get
command does not accept
.B \-\-json
because its output is the stored document itself.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.local/share/planview
Default application data directory on supported Unix systems.
.TP
.B ~/.local/share/planview/profiles/name
Application data directory for a named profile on supported Unix systems.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The command completed successfully.
.TP
.B 1
The command could not complete, or its arguments were invalid.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
plansplease publish ./report.html
plansplease publish --open ./site
plansplease login --cloud-url http://127.0.0.1:3000
plansplease upload ./report.html
plansplease logout
plansplease get http://localhost:4777/<id> > report.html
plansplease status --json
plansplease publish --json ./report.html
plansplease help publish
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR npm (1),
.BR man (1)
